16
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:44,560
You've been on both iOS and Android since very early on and have seen some really interesting things on the Android side, but I did want to kick off on a higher level of just what are the things you think about as a CEO running a super fast growing app that's on both Android and iOS.

17
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:50,400
How do you think about the differences between the two major mobile platforms?

18
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:53,360
Yeah, it's a question top of mind for a lot of topics.

19
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:59,040
To give some context, yeah, Photom started with iOS and later on went on to Android.

20
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:04,880
I think it's one year later, like iOS 2019, Android even 2021.

21
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:07,680
So even like one and a half years between the two.

22
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:14,720
High level, I think the big differences are when I think iOS, I think like super penetration in the American market.

23
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:19,280
When I think about Android, I'm thinking about all the other countries.

24
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:28,720
It's like it's a mix and some countries that are big for mobile subscription like Brazil, Southeast Asia, even Europe where there's a like a good mix.

25
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:34,880
And so I'm thinking, I'm actually thinking like some people might be only focused in the US and in this case, IOS makes sense.

26
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:42,960
If you're like you care about localization, you want to launch in a ton of countries, then Android, you need to do like you can't do IOS only.

27
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:44,000
Was there a lot of demand?

28
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:46,320
Did you hear from users like build us an Android app?

29
